 "text": "Hi, how have you been? It depends how you mean. In vocabulary, Dutch and Norwegian are quite similar, so lot of the same words apply. However, the grammar is quite different. Dutch is much simpler than both Spanish and French, so it' easy to read. Norwegian has some quite unusual words for basic verbs, which can give people a headache. The sounds are entirely different, so an ear for one won't help with the other. People with a bit of Spanish often struggle most. Sorry, I can't answer that. Then give it a year of listening before you read. There are plenty of Dutch movies and series.",
